Replace inline-asm __FD_ZERO with portable C version (GCC 15 compat).

glibc 2.12.1 ships two arch-specific bits/select.h:
  - sysdeps/i386/bits/select.h        (used in i386 builds AND, surprisingly,
                                       installed for x86_64 multilib too)
  - sysdeps/x86_64/bits/select.h      (has __WORDSIZE-conditional stosq/stosl)

For our x86_64 + i386 multilib build, glibc's install picks i386's version
to install in `<sysroot>/usr/include/bits/select.h`. We previously thought
the x86_64 version was active and patched it, but the i386 version is
the one that actually ends up in the sysroot — confirmed by inspecting
the installed file's content (no __WORDSIZE switching, hardcoded "stosl").

The asm in this file:
    int __d0, __d1;                              /* 32-bit */
    __asm__ __volatile__ ("cld; rep; stosl"
                          : "=c" (__d0), "=D" (__d1)
                          : "a" (0), "0" (sizeof (fd_set) / sizeof (__fd_mask)),
                            "1" (&__FDS_BITS (fdsp)[0])
                          : "memory");

When this header is included by code being compiled FOR x86_64 (-m64 by
default for our cross-toolchain), `&__FDS_BITS(...)[0]` is a 64-bit
pointer but C variable `__d1` is declared `int` (32-bit). With `stosl`
suffix `l` (32-bit) and `=D` constraint not specifying width, GCC 15's
register allocator picks bindings that produce e.g. `movl ..., %rdx` —
the assembler rejects this as size mismatch:

    Error: incorrect register `%rdx' used with `l' suffix

Hits readline `input.c` (FD_ZERO calls) and any other code using FD_ZERO.

Fix: use #if 0 to skip the asm version, falling through to the existing
portable C `for` loop in the same file's #else branch. Same change
applied to sysdeps/x86_64/bits/select.h for safety (in case multilib
selection differs across glibc configure paths).

Performance: FD_ZERO is rarely a hot path. Loop with -O2 is essentially
memset — GCC's optimizer recognizes the pattern.

Reference: GCC inline asm operand constraints docs
Reference: glibc 2.13+ rewrote this with __builtin_memset, then 2.34+
           moved to a fully generic implementation removing asm

--- a/sysdeps/i386/bits/select.h	2010-05-04 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ b/sysdeps/i386/bits/select.h	2026-05-09 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
@@ -22,7 +22,9 @@
 #endif


-#if defined __GNUC__ && __GNUC__ >= 2
+/* GCC 15+ register allocator triggers asm operand size mismatch on x86_64
+   multilib build. Force portable C version. */
+#if 0

 # define __FD_ZERO(fdsp) \
   do {									      \
--- a/sysdeps/x86_64/bits/select.h	2010-05-04 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ b/sysdeps/x86_64/bits/select.h	2026-05-09 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
@@ -23,7 +23,9 @@
 #include <bits/wordsize.h>


-#if defined __GNUC__ && __GNUC__ >= 2
+/* GCC 15+ register allocator triggers asm operand size mismatch on x86_64
+   multilib build. Force portable C version. */
+#if 0

 # if __WORDSIZE == 64
 #  define __FD_ZERO_STOS "stosq"
